# GOLDEN persisted rows, captured from origin/main's PRE-REFACTOR serving writers
# (#1142). Do not edit by hand and never regenerate from this branch's row
# builders: that would make the golden test circular.
#
# How these literals were produced (scratch scripts, kept outside the repository):
#   1. `git archive origin/main pipeline/R` (merge base 37a88bf2, before the writers'
#      rows were extracted into lignes_*_persistees builders) into a scratch dir.
#   2. In a scratch R session, every origin/main R file was sourced into an
#      environment whose parent is this branch's namespace, so each function a
#      writer calls is main's: remplacer_scalaire / remplacer_profil_declare /
#      remplacer_series (-> owned_series_postgres_adapter()$replace_dataset) /
#      remplacer_collection / remplacer_aedar (-> publish_aedar_aggregates,
#      ecrire_aedar_comparaison_rows).
#   3. Those writers ran on THIS test suite's fixtures (artefacts_fixture_*,
#      adaptateur_*_artefact) against a recording DBI mock: every data.frame
#      handed to dbWriteTable() was kept as is; rows sent through
#      `INSERT INTO t(cols) VALUES(...)` / `UPDATE t SET col=$1` / JSON
#      `jsonb_to_recordset` batches were decoded into the same table shape.
#      Marker tables (*_publication, resource_publication*) are not resource rows.
#   4. dput(). The only post-processing is representational: PostgreSQL array
#      literals were re-spelled `{a,b}` ({"a","b"} is the same array).
# AEDAR is dense over the whole TYPEQU registry (2350 aggregate rows and 293280
# comparison-group rows), too large to inline: tables over 200 rows are pinned by
# row count, sorted column set, two literal head rows and a SHA-256 of the canonical
# text of every row (see .digest_lignes() in test-adoption-persisted-rows.R).
